.TH SIBYLFS 4
.SH NAME
sibylfs \- sessions of a coding agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sibylfs
[
.B -D
] [
.B -d
.I model
] [
.B -m
.I mtpt
] [
.B -o
.I ocurl
] [
.B -s
.I srvname
] [
.B -u
.I url
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Sibylfs
serves the sessions of
.IR sibyl (1)
on
.I mtpt
.RB ( /mnt/sibyl ),
laid out as
.B /net
is, and posts them as
.BI /srv/ srvname
with
.BR -s .
.I Acmestart
mounts one before Acme starts, so Acme and what it runs share it.
Each session runs its own agent loop against Anthropic's Messages API, through
.IR webfs (4),
or OpenCode Go's for a model named
.BI opencode-go/ id\f1;
.B -u
and
.B -o
name other places for them, and
.B -d
the model a session starts with (else
.BR $sibylmodel ).
The key is factotum's,
.B proto=pass
.B service=anthropic
or
.BR service=opencode .
.B doc/sibyl.md
has the rest.
.TF n/call/k/status
.TP
.B clone
Opening it makes a session,
.IR n ;
the fid is
.IB n /ctl\f1's.
.TP
.IB n /ctl
Reading gives
.IR n ,
then the model, the key's service, the effort, the role, the prompt file and the state.
Writing takes
.BI model " m" \f1,
.BI effort " e" \f1,
.BI role " r"
.RB ( /lib/sibyl/ \fIr\fP's
instructions too),
.BI prompt " file" \f1,
.BR cancel ,
.BI steer " text"
and
.BR hangup ,
which ends the session at once.
.TP
.IB n /data
A turn is what is written on one open, sent when it is closed; a read gives the reply as it
comes, to the end of the turn a reader has not finished, and a turn that failed gives its
error there.
Opened to read and write,
.B data
is an aside, as
.BR /net/cs
is a query and its answer: what is written is the turn, sent at the first read, which gives
its reply; the session's other readers pass over it.
Asides wait behind the session's turns.
.TP
.IB n /ask
Questions, from one fid to another.
A fid that writes first asks: what it writes is the question, whole at its first read, which
waits for the answer and gives it.
A fid that reads first answers: its reads give the oldest question no other fid has, to its
end, and what it writes, to its close, is the answer.
.I Sibyl -i
answers its session's questions, from
.IR quibble ,
by sending each as an aside.
.TP
.IB n /event
A line for each call,
.IB k " rc" \f1,
and
.IB k " cancel"
when a cancel ends one being run.
A line read is gone.
.TP
.IB n /call/ k /cmd
The call's command.
.TP
.IB n /call/ k /out
Its output: the runner's writes add to it, and a read waits for more until
.TP
.IB n /call/ k /status
is written, which ends the call.
.TP
.IB n /usage
The session's tokens and their cost.
.PD
.PP
A session ends when the last of its files is closed.
.B -D
prints the 9P messages.
.SH SOURCE
plan9web's
.B src/cmd/sibylfs
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR sibyl (1),
.IR searchfs (4),
.IR webfs (4)
